# Pong

## Sound API
- play PCM embedded data pointed to by file wrapper
ac97.c: `void play(struct file pcm_data);`

# Panic
- panic doesn't seem to print to the screen for some reason.

# Scheduler
- create a scheduler process
- hook timer ISR to return execution to the scheduler process
- rewrite yield() to not jump into scheduler, but halt until
ready (this should be safe enough to work with now, but we'll
want to hand off the rest of the time slice to another process
for a robust solution.)
- don't pass pagetable by value; refactor it to an addrspace struct

# Memory
- remove cr4 references from process-specific code.
- communicate that cr3 is usually the *address bits*, since
the register values holds more than just that.
